# inc-cmo5: seed-7 human paladin, literal h twice on the toggle page.
# First entry stays on page 1; TAB reaches the toggle on page 2.
#
# inc-stzd: seed 7's first offered attribute set (picked below with the
# literal "a") bundles a free "Bonus Feat: Iron Will" -- src/Create.cpp:1690
# draws that bonus from random(FT_LAST - FT_FIRST) + FT_FIRST, so adding a
# feat to the table (inc-08js, FT_LAST 362 -> 363) changed what every seed's
# draw lands on; Iron Will is simply this seed's new answer, and HasFeat
# then excludes it from the manual "Choose a feat" list regardless of the
# Hide/Show toggle. Picking Iron Will by name below would therefore fail on
# ANY tree with a different feat-table size, Cannibalism or not -- so this
# script no longer picks it manually; it is already on the sheet via the
# bonus, and the two manual picks below are by name, immune to table size.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Human"
@choose "Athletics"      # first racial skill
@choose "Diplomacy"      # second racial skill
@choose "Paladin"
@choose "Erich"

a       # Attributes: the first of the offered sets
a       # Alignment:  the first offered

@dump:initial-feats
@until "(Show All Feats)" TAB
@dump:toggle-before
h
@dump:toggle-on
h
@dump:toggle-off
@until "Great Fortitude" TAB
@choose "Great Fortitude"
@until "Alertness" TAB
@choose "Alertness"
# Iron Will came free with the attribute set; a further pick is offered only
# on the fixed build (inc-cmo5). Whatever it offers, take the top entry --
# the sheet check below does not care which extra feat this is, only that
# Battlefield Inspiration (the toggle bug's own symptom) is not it.
@while "Choose a feat" a

# Skill Manager. RIGHT spends a rank on the selected skill and stops at that
# skill's maximum; DOWN moves to the next skill. The loop matches the stars
# that count unspent ranks, not the header, which stays on screen when the
# pool is empty and so would never become false.
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks

@while "wish to worship" y
@while "personality archetype" a

ESC     # dismiss the arrival room description

d
@until "Great Fortitude" PGDN
PGDN*5
@dump:sheet-feats
ESC
@quit
